#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248211 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "63080bb8-7a6a-505d-813a-e6c99d337064" :knowledge-point/title "Adding and Subtracting a Number and a Rational Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40831578-ff21-558c-89b8-520eb3865c9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2h-1}{h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248213} {:answer/id #uuid "22555531-2d92-54be-8c5a-ef1a04e70bd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{h-3}{h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248214} {:answer/id #uuid "6d7eda36-c6fd-572b-9acd-285549208452" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3(2h-1)}{h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248215} {:answer/id #uuid "5b48c39f-6466-5150-9c81-103e929cfff3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2h+1}{h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248216} {:answer/id #uuid "3e022e83-0361-56e3-97f7-a1b9916772e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3(2h+1)}{h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248217}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d7eda36-c6fd-572b-9acd-285549208452" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3(2h-1)}{h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248215} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cc2b2e9-11aa-5acb-9238-ecd67f93b5fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248212}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1499037e-a606-58e5-b3be-b1c588e43b7e" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-113219" :question/problem "Write $5+\\frac{h-3}{h}$ as a single fraction." :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that $5=\\frac{5}{1},$ we can write the expression as\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{1}+\\frac{h-3}{h}.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn order to add the two fractions, we need them to have a common denominator. So, we put both fractions over a common denominator of $h$ by multiplying the top and bottom of the first fraction by $h:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{1}+\\frac{h-3}{h} & = \\\\ \\frac{h}{h}\\cdot \\frac{5}{1}+\\frac{h-3}{h} & = \\\\ \\frac{5h}{h}+\\frac{h-3}{h}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we add the fractions and simplify the result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5h}{h}+\\frac{h-3}{h} & = \\\\ \\frac{5h+h-3}{h} & = \\\\ \\frac{6h-3}{h} & = \\\\ \\frac{3(2h-1)}{h}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248218 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "63080bb8-7a6a-505d-813a-e6c99d337064" :knowledge-point/title "Adding and Subtracting a Number and a Rational Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98fac445-356a-51e0-b888-496a7ae95742" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8k-3}{k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248220} {:answer/id #uuid "9bb2a8b2-4457-5aec-a75e-59ad6db210b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4k+3}{k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248221} {:answer/id #uuid "a84b2eab-b5a6-5fb1-b468-bd9134470196" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4k-1}{k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248222} {:answer/id #uuid "bf7979c6-4748-5675-9411-96254bee1d3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3(k-1)}{k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248223} {:answer/id #uuid "c4a8c1b4-00b2-522d-a935-677d003a19ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3(k+1)}{k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248224}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bb2a8b2-4457-5aec-a75e-59ad6db210b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4k+3}{k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248221} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf1f80a0-b455-513e-92e2-e43df47b271b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248219}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "191f0018-0145-5873-a8dd-22bae45a6fd5" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-113221" :question/problem "Write $6+\\frac{3-2k}{k}$ as a single fraction." :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that $6=\\frac{6}{1},$ we can write the expression as\n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{1}+\\frac{3-2k}{k}.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn order to add the two fractions, we need them to have a common denominator. So, we put both fractions over a common denominator of $k$ by multiplying the top and bottom of the first fraction by $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6}{1}+\\frac{3-2k}{k} & = \\\\ \\frac{k}{k}\\cdot \\frac{6}{1}+\\frac{3-2k}{k} & = \\\\ \\frac{6k}{k}+\\frac{3-2k}{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we add the fractions and simplify the result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6k}{k}+\\frac{3-2k}{k} & = \\\\ \\frac{6k+3-2k}{k} & = \\\\ \\frac{4k+3}{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248225 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3db20b82-9561-5c54-8e12-8914bb6747c3" :knowledge-point/title "Adding and Subtracting Rational Expressions With No Common Factors in the Denominators"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35acb02d-3a88-5e3e-b046-6c4c14422ac2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4z-3}{z(z-3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248227} {:answer/id #uuid "29d09dec-7f83-5338-a72c-f34b18541e6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{z}{z-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248228} {:answer/id #uuid "421b6f34-6602-54be-ad0d-22d342daebc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{z(z-3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248229} {:answer/id #uuid "fcc0922a-4cf3-566a-b30b-f6ad166d2300" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4z-6}{z-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248230} {:answer/id #uuid "8fe43b00-080f-5dd0-b421-3b9cc5166618" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{z}{z(z-3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248231}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35acb02d-3a88-5e3e-b046-6c4c14422ac2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4z-3}{z(z-3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248227} :answer-field/id #uuid "06b71a9b-fa43-5f7c-abe8-85073e56921d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248226}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7b31894d-8a98-5cb2-800f-c6e12082fad0" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-70357" :question/problem "$\\frac{1}{z}+\\frac{3}{z-3}=$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we need to put the fractions over a common denominator of $z(z-3),$ since there are no common factors in either denominator that we can exploit.\n\nTo do this, we multiply the top and bottom of the first fraction by $z-3$, and the top and bottom of the second fraction by $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{z}+\\frac{3}{z-3} & = \\\\ \\frac{z-3}{z-3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{z}+\\frac{z}{z}\\cdot \\frac{3}{z-3} & = \\\\ \\frac{z-3}{z(z-3)}+\\frac{3z}{z(z-3)} & = \\\\ \\frac{z-3+3z}{z(z-3)} & = \\\\ \\frac{4z-3}{z(z-3)} & \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248232 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3db20b82-9561-5c54-8e12-8914bb6747c3" :knowledge-point/title "Adding and Subtracting Rational Expressions With No Common Factors in the Denominators"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "401d2718-887e-554b-8971-8d418fd98913" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x-3}{x(2x-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248234} {:answer/id #uuid "47c36c84-8d28-5f3e-a8b5-3b46722145e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248235} {:answer/id #uuid "755a0bb5-46da-5d71-9713-4b80a1a22c19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x+3}{2x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248236} {:answer/id #uuid "a60e8bb7-568a-5e71-a040-f605250d504c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x+6}{x(2x-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248237} {:answer/id #uuid "0127dede-9d83-58c2-b5c8-4f0df8f08afc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{x(2x-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248238}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0127dede-9d83-58c2-b5c8-4f0df8f08afc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{x(2x-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248238} :answer-field/id #uuid "07dc012d-a667-5954-91d9-7aa4361493e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248233}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4a571faa-9b3c-5aee-961d-64e751de7349" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-70359" :question/problem "$\\frac{6}{2x-1}-\\frac{3}{x}=$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we need to put the fractions over a common denominator of $x(2x-1),$ since there are no common factors in either denominator that we can exploit. \n\nTo do this, we multiply the top and bottom of the first fraction by $x,$ and the top and bottom of the second fraction by $2x-1:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6}{2x-1}-\\frac{3}{x} & = \\\\ \\frac{x}{x}\\cdot \\frac{6}{2x-1}-\\frac{2x-1}{2x-1}\\cdot \\frac{3}{x} & = \\\\ \\frac{6x}{x(2x-1)}-\\frac{3(2x-1)}{x(2x-1)} & = \\\\ \\frac{6x-3(2x-1)}{x(2x-1)} & = \\\\ \\frac{6x-6x+3}{x(2x-1)} & = \\\\ \\frac{3}{x(2x-1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248239 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3db20b82-9561-5c54-8e12-8914bb6747c3" :knowledge-point/title "Adding and Subtracting Rational Expressions With No Common Factors in the Denominators"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e564ff2c-1719-5c57-a761-db1d381e7749" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10xy}{(x-6)(2x+3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248241} {:answer/id #uuid "04a6629e-4cf6-552a-a443-b4d20c83c7ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12y}{(x-6)(2x+3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248242} {:answer/id #uuid "60ec7ccd-50ef-5dbc-903a-94cb2981b417" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6xy+12y}{(x-6)(2x+3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248243} {:answer/id #uuid "71ade2bf-a7c6-5e1e-bc8f-23dd89871f4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6y+12}{(x-6)(2x+3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248244} {:answer/id #uuid "78f6d37c-e0f5-5d3b-b8d5-ca2a5a7272ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6y}{(x-6)(2x+3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248245}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e564ff2c-1719-5c57-a761-db1d381e7749" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10xy}{(x-6)(2x+3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248241} :answer-field/id #uuid "74e9046d-f22f-53e9-ba26-6db5af2a6b6c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248240}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "122985a1-7e86-5493-b392-952256a980d8" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-70360" :question/problem "$\\frac{4y}{x-6}+\\frac{2y}{2x+3}=$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we need to put the fractions over a common denominator of $(x-6)(2x+3),$ since there are no common factors in either denominator that we can exploit. \n\nTo do this, we multiply the top and bottom of the first fraction by $2x+3,$ and the top and bottom of the second fraction by $x-6:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4y}{x-6}+\\frac{2y}{2x+3} & = \\\\ \\frac{2x+3}{2x+3}\\cdot \\frac{4y}{x-6}+\\frac{x-6}{x-6}\\cdot \\frac{2y}{2x+3} & = \\\\ \\frac{4y(2x+3)}{(x-6)(2x+3)}+\\frac{2y(x-6)}{(x-6)(2x+3)} & = \\\\ \\frac{4y(2x+3)+2y(x-6)}{(x-6)(2x+3)} & = \\\\ \\frac{8xy+12y+2xy-12y}{(x-6)(2x+3)} & = \\\\ \\frac{10xy}{(x-6)(2x+3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
